WEBVTT

00:37.300 --> 00:39.310
Got you!

00:48.220 --> 00:51.110
What was that blood he spat out?

00:51.770 --> 00:53.110
Poison?

00:53.640 --> 00:55.000
What's this?

00:55.000 --> 00:56.570
You're strong.

00:57.270 --> 00:59.470
That's no fun.

01:02.990 --> 01:04.530
Straw Doll Technique:

01:04.890 --> 01:06.080
Resonance!

01:25.560 --> 01:26.760
How many of them are there?

01:27.310 --> 01:30.400
We should just keep going 
like it's whack-a-mole, huh?

01:30.400 --> 01:31.270
Yeah.

01:31.630 --> 01:32.690
Keep going.

01:32.690 --> 01:34.850
Keep exorcising them for me.

01:34.850 --> 01:36.780
We'll crush every last one of them.

01:37.270 --> 01:39.000
It likely won't retaliate.

01:40.150 --> 01:43.890
You mean its main body 
doesn't have much offense

01:43.890 --> 01:46.680
since its technique covers a 
wide area, even limited as it is?

01:47.160 --> 01:48.980
I'm only saying it's likely.

01:50.050 --> 01:52.550
All the things we were worried aboutâ€”
its technique's range,

01:52.550 --> 01:54.530
the number of victims, the barrierâ€”

01:54.970 --> 01:57.870
All of those are subtracting 
from its main body.

01:58.440 --> 01:59.500
We're lucky.

02:00.230 --> 02:02.890
We'll be able to exorcise it quickly, then.

02:04.290 --> 02:07.680
Which means... the real 
problem comes afterward.

02:16.280 --> 02:17.400
Kugisaki!

02:17.910 --> 02:19.360
I'll be fine.

02:20.080 --> 02:22.610
You just whack the mole.

02:25.200 --> 02:26.220
Damn it!

02:26.680 --> 02:28.780
She gets sucked away so often!

02:29.380 --> 02:30.960
But what was that just now?

02:32.230 --> 02:33.130
The mole?

02:34.090 --> 02:35.440
That earlier one?

02:36.520 --> 02:38.060
It's neither!

02:39.330 --> 02:40.310
Kugisaki?

02:40.310 --> 02:43.470
Oh, hey, it's my older brother!

02:44.000 --> 02:46.900
Me, too!

02:50.810 --> 02:51.770
It fled?!

02:52.220 --> 02:53.350
Should I let it go?

02:53.350 --> 02:54.770
Chase after it!

02:54.770 --> 02:58.780
Kugisaki and that thing both 
went outside the barrier!

02:59.200 --> 03:02.790
She might be battling against something 
more troublesome than we expected!

03:02.790 --> 03:05.250
In contrast, things are far 
easier here than anticipated!

03:05.250 --> 03:06.770
I can handle this by myself!

03:07.080 --> 03:09.290
Prioritize Kugisaki! Go after it!

03:10.320 --> 03:11.690
If things get bad in here,

03:12.740 --> 03:14.640
then you come out, too.

03:23.540 --> 03:24.390
Why, you...

03:24.390 --> 03:25.680
Don't touch me!

03:31.900 --> 03:34.320
You're a woman?

03:34.320 --> 03:37.650
Well, pardon me.

03:38.900 --> 03:43.440
We brothers were tasked with an errand.

03:44.650 --> 03:49.200
But killing jujutsu sorcerers 
isn't part of that.

03:49.660 --> 03:52.660
If you withdraw, we'll let you escape,

03:54.300 --> 03:55.670
young lady.

03:56.100 --> 03:57.170
An errand?

03:57.600 --> 04:01.160
Hm? I presumed you were 
on the same errand.

04:01.680 --> 04:03.570
A cursed spirit? A curse user?

04:03.570 --> 04:05.170
Which is he?

04:05.170 --> 04:07.170
And what is that smell?

04:21.490 --> 04:22.490
Last one!

04:25.320 --> 04:28.490
Your sneak attack's too simple.

04:32.230 --> 04:35.230
I told you, it's too simple.

04:41.940 --> 04:43.670
Did I exorcise them all?

04:44.910 --> 04:47.700
That takes care of Tsumiki for now.

04:49.030 --> 04:50.220
Now to...

04:59.540 --> 05:01.010
One survived?

05:01.660 --> 05:03.670
That wasn't its main body just now?

05:04.420 --> 05:06.010
The barrier hasn't collapsed, either.

05:06.010 --> 05:07.010
What?

05:11.320 --> 05:15.860
I shouldn't try too hard to find logic 
in a cursed spirit's behavioral patterns,

05:17.160 --> 05:19.660
but that fact had been 
nagging me this whole time.

05:20.430 --> 05:27.020
Why did it just start killing 
humans it had marked now?

05:28.260 --> 05:30.760
The first one was killed in June.

05:32.260 --> 05:33.560
And in June...

05:38.100 --> 05:41.010
Our objective here...

05:41.300 --> 05:44.490
is to retrieve Sukuna's finger.

07:07.060 --> 07:10.810
JUJUTSU KAISEN

07:19.290 --> 07:26.370
Episode 23: The Origin of Blind Obedience - 2 -

07:19.290 --> 07:26.370
Episode 23: The Origin of Blind Obedience - 2 -

07:19.600 --> 07:21.480
Some have a presence 
that's too overwhelming.

07:22.240 --> 07:24.030
Some keep very quiet.

07:24.420 --> 07:27.330
Some have already been 
absorbed by a cursed spirit.

07:28.470 --> 07:30.290
This is resonance.

07:31.200 --> 07:33.440
Sukuna's finger kept its power repressed

07:33.440 --> 07:36.210
within the cursed spirit 
that had absorbed it,

07:36.530 --> 07:37.780
but back in June,

07:38.210 --> 07:41.720
when Sukuna manifested in Itadori, 
it released its cursed energy.

07:43.670 --> 07:45.110
It looks the same

07:46.980 --> 07:49.820
as the one from the juvenile detention center, 
but it's probably several degrees...

07:56.270 --> 07:57.400
stronger!

08:07.780 --> 08:08.630
Nue!

08:14.570 --> 08:17.200
Okay, I win again.

08:18.570 --> 08:20.410
This is unusual.

08:20.410 --> 08:22.850
You rarely ask me to train you, Megumi.

08:23.220 --> 08:25.650
Are you in a rush after Yuji surpassed you?

08:26.320 --> 08:29.760
Well, beggars can't be choosers.

08:30.270 --> 08:33.280
It bothers you that much to rely on me?

08:34.040 --> 08:35.730
Megumi, listen.

08:35.730 --> 08:40.290
I think you have just as much ability 
and potential as Yuji does.

08:40.790 --> 08:43.670
The problem is just your mindset.

08:44.240 --> 08:45.290
Megumi,

08:45.290 --> 08:48.090
you don't know how to 
bring out your best, do you?

08:48.840 --> 08:50.290
Huh?

08:50.730 --> 08:53.410
Are you saying I haven't 
been giving it my best?

08:53.410 --> 08:56.380
I'm not saying you haven't.
I'm saying you can't.

08:56.890 --> 08:59.100
For example, in the baseball game the other day...

08:59.940 --> 09:01.760
Why did you go for a sacrifice bunt?

09:06.110 --> 09:07.940
Did you want Nobara to advance the bases,

09:07.940 --> 09:09.930
even if it meant you'd be out?

09:10.460 --> 09:11.810
That's a splendid attitude,

09:12.710 --> 09:16.060
but Yuji and I would 
always go for a home run.

09:19.240 --> 09:21.610
I'm not saying a bunt is bad.

09:21.620 --> 09:23.620
Baseball is a team sport,

09:23.620 --> 09:25.910
and everyone has their role to play.

09:25.910 --> 09:28.660
But jujutsu sorcery is an individual sport.

09:29.200 --> 09:31.710
Coordinating with other sorcerers 
is important, isn't it?

09:32.360 --> 09:33.630
Sure.

09:34.020 --> 09:37.030
But no matter how many 
allies you have around you,

09:37.930 --> 09:40.050
when you die, you'll be alone.

09:41.250 --> 09:45.270
You can only piece together 
undervalued data on yourself and others.

09:46.180 --> 09:50.430
You can't imagine a stronger 
future version of yourself.

09:50.890 --> 09:52.880
Maybe that's because of your trump card?

09:53.670 --> 09:55.430
You believe that in the worst case,

09:55.430 --> 09:57.590
you can resolve everything 
at the cost of your life.

09:59.140 --> 10:01.120
But at that point, forget about me.

10:01.120 --> 10:02.750
You'll never even measure up to Nanami.

10:03.850 --> 10:07.060
Dying to win and risking death to win...

10:10.730 --> 10:14.060
are completely different, Megumi.

10:15.560 --> 10:16.870
Give it your best.

10:17.380 --> 10:19.000
Be greedier.

10:28.820 --> 10:30.880
How many seconds was I unconscious?

10:31.810 --> 10:33.790
My Demon Dog's destroyed...

10:33.790 --> 10:36.480
no, the technique was released.

10:39.940 --> 10:43.960
This is it for me.

10:45.710 --> 10:50.080
Sacred treasure, swing...

10:55.980 --> 10:58.170
What a waste of talent.

11:02.000 --> 11:03.400
Screw it!

11:04.660 --> 11:07.160
A jujutsu sorcerer's growth curve

11:07.590 --> 11:10.300
isn't necessarily a gentle slope.

11:11.530 --> 11:15.260
Back then, why did you run?

11:16.760 --> 11:19.370
Spit out the entire depths of my shadow...

11:20.430 --> 11:23.050
Worry about a specific structure later,

11:24.380 --> 11:27.380
and just push it out as soon 
as I collect the cursed energy.

11:28.610 --> 11:33.250
Imagine a future version of myself 
who's freely surpassed my limits!

11:34.070 --> 11:35.450
I'll do it!

11:35.850 --> 11:37.410
With a strong foundation,

11:37.890 --> 11:40.330
and a little bit of sense and imagination,

11:41.050 --> 11:44.260
it just takes the slightest trigger 
to change a person.

11:45.430 --> 11:47.800
Domain Expansion:

11:52.850 --> 11:55.350
Chimera Shadow Garden!

11:58.420 --> 11:59.720
It's incomplete!

12:00.260 --> 12:02.210
It's ugly work at best.

12:02.650 --> 12:05.030
But for now, that's fine!

12:21.050 --> 12:22.720
Broaden it...

12:25.150 --> 12:26.760
more freely!

12:29.890 --> 12:31.010
The interpretation

12:34.080 --> 12:35.560
of the technique!

12:59.450 --> 13:04.960
Demon Dog Totality's claws 
were able to injure that thing.

13:08.470 --> 13:11.430
They'd have no trouble piercing through 
you when you're caught off-guard.

13:23.700 --> 13:24.980
I'm tired.

13:28.270 --> 13:31.600
Now, where are those guys?

13:34.820 --> 13:35.870
Good!

13:36.580 --> 13:38.760
That's good!

13:54.140 --> 13:56.930
JUJUTSU KAISEN

13:59.600 --> 14:01.940
JUJUTSU KAISEN

14:04.310 --> 14:07.680
There's one fundamental rule 
for interacting with others.

14:08.770 --> 14:10.140
Do you know what that is?

14:10.140 --> 14:11.820
I don't.

14:12.590 --> 14:15.420
It's "I won't kill you,

14:15.420 --> 14:18.780
so please don't kill me, either."

14:19.170 --> 14:21.340
You can substitute "kill" 
for anything you please.

14:21.790 --> 14:25.510
The point is drawing a line where you agree 
not to infringe on the other person.

14:25.510 --> 14:28.040
In order for both people to exist together,

14:28.040 --> 14:29.400
they need that rule.

14:30.010 --> 14:31.830
Breaking that rule, swaggering about,

14:31.830 --> 14:33.970
and having others trying not to anger you

14:35.140 --> 14:37.220
must have felt real pleasant.

14:39.280 --> 14:41.940
Next time you do it in 
front of me, I'll kill you.

14:42.500 --> 14:45.100
What did we ever do to you?

14:45.500 --> 14:47.220
Figure it out yourself,

14:47.220 --> 14:48.610
or go die.

14:48.610 --> 14:49.600
Hey!

14:51.020 --> 14:54.120
T-T-T-T-Today's the day I tell 
off Ikezawa and his buddies!

14:54.120 --> 14:57.240
I'm not their gofer anymore!

14:57.240 --> 14:58.940
You can do it, Aida-shi!

14:58.940 --> 15:02.000
But I might become their next target,

15:02.000 --> 15:04.120
so don't try too hard, Aida-shi!

15:04.120 --> 15:06.080
Hey, come on, fatty!

15:06.080 --> 15:07.510
I'm changing the line!

15:07.510 --> 15:10.840
I'll tell them this fatty is my 
replacement starting today!

15:10.840 --> 15:12.750
You'd sell your friend out, Aida-shi?!

15:12.750 --> 15:14.080
Shut up!

15:14.740 --> 15:15.990
Megumi.

15:19.520 --> 15:20.280
Huh?

15:20.280 --> 15:23.010
Isn't that Ikezawa and his 
buddies piled up over there?

15:23.730 --> 15:26.090
You said you wouldn't fight anymore.

15:27.260 --> 15:29.020
Don't act like you're my guardian.

15:30.580 --> 15:32.520
I hate bad people.

15:35.880 --> 15:38.780
They act so damn superior when 
their empathy and imagination

15:38.780 --> 15:41.140
are as empty as a vacant lot.

15:42.140 --> 15:43.760
I can't deal with good people.

15:44.740 --> 15:46.970
They forgive those bad people.

15:48.230 --> 15:51.020
Then they view the act of 
forgiveness as a noble thing.

15:53.360 --> 15:54.810
Makes me want to vomit.

15:56.130 --> 15:58.360
Tsumiki's a model example of a good person.

16:00.240 --> 16:01.510
You disgust me.

16:05.940 --> 16:07.460
Oh, sorry.

16:07.460 --> 16:09.190
I didn't think it'd spill out.

16:10.410 --> 16:12.270
When I was in first grade,

16:13.100 --> 16:16.040
my father and Tsumiki's mother,

16:16.040 --> 16:18.490
one parent each, hooked up...

16:19.620 --> 16:21.190
and then vanished without a trace.

16:22.760 --> 16:25.630
A suspicious white-haired man told us...

16:25.630 --> 16:27.460
You know, your dad...

16:27.460 --> 16:31.120
He's from the Zen'in Clan, 
a big clan among jujutsu sorcerers,

16:31.530 --> 16:33.980
but they're such good-for-nothings, 
it freaks even me out.

16:33.980 --> 16:36.580
Your father left the clan to have you.

16:37.510 --> 16:39.140
Megumi-kun,

16:39.140 --> 16:44.550
your father was saving you as the ultimate 
card to use against the Zen'in clan.

16:45.510 --> 16:46.740
Pisses you off, doesn't it?

16:47.940 --> 16:50.650
That solved the mystery of how 
they got the funds to disappear.

16:51.180 --> 16:53.650
Apparently, I had been sold 
to that Zen'in clan.

16:54.450 --> 16:56.330
Yeah, it pisses me off.

16:56.330 --> 16:58.860
Especially your lack of tact about it.

17:00.110 --> 17:04.160
Plus, that irritating man stopped 
my sale to the Zen'in clan,

17:04.670 --> 17:08.420
and used the promise that I would work 
as a jujutsu sorcerer as collateral

17:08.420 --> 17:12.710
to get financial aid from 
Jujutsu High to support us both.

17:15.410 --> 17:17.120
What's this jujutsu sorcerer crap, anyway?

17:17.120 --> 17:18.280
It's bullshit.

17:18.670 --> 17:21.410
Who the hell would I ever save?

17:21.410 --> 17:22.680
Hey, Tsumiki!

17:22.680 --> 17:24.480
What are you doing?

17:24.480 --> 17:26.110
Megumi-kun, ciao!

17:26.440 --> 17:27.640
Nothing.

17:27.640 --> 17:28.770
Hey, hold on.

17:28.770 --> 17:32.150
So did you give any thought 
to the test of courage?

17:32.150 --> 17:35.040
I don't want to go, but I'll go 
because I'm worried about you.

17:35.690 --> 17:37.870
Shortly after I started ninth grade,

17:37.870 --> 17:39.960
Tsumiki was cursed.

17:40.830 --> 17:42.980
The identity was unknown.
The origin was unknown.

17:43.520 --> 17:46.170
But apparently there were several 
victims of the same curse nationwide.

17:47.500 --> 17:50.330
All I found out was that 
nobody knew anything,

17:50.330 --> 17:52.520
and Tsumiki was left bedridden.

17:53.620 --> 17:56.080
If I have the time to curse someone,

17:56.080 --> 17:58.630
I'd rather spend it thinking 
about those precious to me.

17:59.190 --> 18:01.530
She always smiled and spouted pretty ideals.

18:02.540 --> 18:05.360
Not forgiving people isn't a bad thing.

18:05.360 --> 18:07.560
That's just part of your kindness, isn't it?

18:08.600 --> 18:10.900
She even accepted my disposition.

18:12.230 --> 18:17.050
Yet Tsumiki would get genuinely 
angry whenever I hurt someone, too.

18:18.110 --> 18:19.970
That irritated me because

18:20.700 --> 18:23.570
I thought it was hypocritical in light 
of her leave-others-be policy,

18:24.780 --> 18:28.900
but now I realize I had the wrong idea.

18:29.840 --> 18:32.660
Just as I choose who I save,

18:32.660 --> 18:35.200
she was choosing me to worry about.

18:36.250 --> 18:37.290
I'm sorry.

18:37.740 --> 18:39.020
I was just a kid.

18:39.640 --> 18:40.920
I'll apologize.

18:42.210 --> 18:45.360
So wake up already, stupid sister.

18:46.360 --> 18:49.990
Damn, my head hurts...

18:51.310 --> 18:54.520
This Yasohachi Bridge curse 
was just overlapping the other one.

18:55.200 --> 18:59.150
I doubt the curse that put Tsumiki 
into a coma was undone.

19:01.290 --> 19:05.960
Now, how do I break the news 
about the finger... to... Itadori...

19:09.950 --> 19:11.950
m 0 0 l 0 -150 l 98 -150 l 96 0

19:09.950 --> 19:11.950
Fushiguro
Fell
Asleep

19:14.220 --> 19:16.890
A huge presence suddenly appeared.

19:16.890 --> 19:19.460
Did Sukuna's finger leave the barrier?

19:20.510 --> 19:24.300
If a sorcerer exorcised the finger's host,

19:25.230 --> 19:26.960
they're quite good.

19:27.530 --> 19:29.400
But even if the finger's...

19:29.400 --> 19:32.540
Even if the special-grade 
cursed spirit was defeated,

19:33.400 --> 19:35.410
they wouldn't come out unscathed.

19:35.950 --> 19:37.460
I hope they're okay.

19:39.900 --> 19:41.190
I misspoke.

19:41.190 --> 19:44.560
Please forget what I just said.

19:44.850 --> 19:46.050
Hold on!

19:46.530 --> 19:49.160
He's going after the finger!

19:49.690 --> 19:51.960
You think you can mock me 
by running like that

19:51.960 --> 19:54.640
and still get away from me?

19:55.000 --> 19:58.470
I'm a bit insecure about my back, you see.

19:58.470 --> 20:00.000
This is your warning.

20:00.330 --> 20:03.010
If you see my back, I'll killâ€”

20:02.010 --> 20:04.130
Oh, Kugisaki!

20:04.470 --> 20:06.010
Oh, brother!

20:06.010 --> 20:13.380
Y-Y-Y-You saw, didn't you?!

20:13.380 --> 20:14.630
Huh?! Who?!

20:13.380 --> 20:14.930
Sorry, brother!

20:14.630 --> 20:15.920
Sorry, I guess?

20:14.930 --> 20:15.700
It wasn't on purpose!

20:15.700 --> 20:17.190
It wasn't on purpose!

20:17.190 --> 20:20.680
I'll kill you!

20:25.260 --> 20:28.020
Then why are you dressed like that?

20:28.020 --> 20:29.860
Is that the source of this weird smell?

20:30.120 --> 20:31.540
Because it gets musty!

20:32.080 --> 20:36.290
Rot Technique, Supreme Art: Wing King!

20:38.670 --> 20:40.050
Death...

20:41.290 --> 20:44.590
by Wasp!

22:14.930 --> 22:17.440
Juju Stroll

22:18.950 --> 22:20.750
Sensei!

22:20.750 --> 22:23.770
Kugisaki!

22:22.830 --> 22:23.770
Huh?

22:24.200 --> 22:26.140
So annoying.

22:26.140 --> 22:28.750
It's too hot for your craziness.

22:28.750 --> 22:31.030
Fushiguro's getting hit on!

22:32.630 --> 22:34.100
Formation B!

22:34.100 --> 22:35.330
Roger!

22:36.980 --> 22:39.530
Fushiguro-kyun!

22:39.530 --> 22:41.110
Who is that woman?!

22:41.110 --> 22:43.660
Have you forgotten the night 
you toasted to my eyes?

22:43.660 --> 22:47.910
Was it all a lie when you said your time 
with me was the most enjoyable of all?!

22:45.920 --> 22:49.210
That night! That night!

22:48.350 --> 22:49.550
What?

22:49.550 --> 22:50.820
Seriously, what?

22:52.300 --> 22:54.730
Could you not touch him so casually, please,

22:54.730 --> 22:56.310
you homewreckers?!

22:56.690 --> 23:02.260
Megumi-chan has violin practice with me now.

23:02.860 --> 23:05.330
Let's go home, Megumi-chan.

23:05.330 --> 23:08.990
Today I'll have you master 
"Twinkle Twinkle Little Star."

23:09.450 --> 23:10.470
It's okay.

23:10.470 --> 23:12.100
Don't mind them. Just go ahead.

23:12.100 --> 23:13.760
The station's straight ahead.

23:13.760 --> 23:15.450
Thank you so much.

23:15.450 --> 23:16.310
Huh?

23:17.090 --> 23:19.010
Okay, seriously, what is this?

23:19.680 --> 23:22.130
Could you stop? You're embarrassing me.

23:25.340 --> 23:26.880
Explain!

23:28.920 --> 23:29.880
Ow!

23:36.430 --> 23:39.890
Episode 24:
The Origin of Blind Obedience - 3 -
